{#- THE PAGE AS IT WILL LOOK, beside the words (2026-10-07; beside Pages as
   the staff Site Creator has it, 2026-10-20): the page these words are on,
   with what is typed drawn into it before it is saved, and its sections as
   they are arranged (2026-10-21). A link pressed in it opens that page; a
   section pressed in it opens that section (admin-content.js). Shown where
   there is room for it (admin.css AREAS). `data-v` is the version of what
   draws the sections in it — the templates, Nunjucks, the frame's
   arithmetic — so a change to them is fetched fresh. -#}
<aside class="c-preview" id="cPreview" data-device="wide" data-v="{{ previewV }}" hidden>
  <div class="c-prev-bar">
    <span class="c-prev-on-site" data-i18n="ws.onSite">On the Site</span>
    <span class="c-prev-url" id="cPrevUrl"></span>
    <span class="ws-dev" role="group" data-i18n-attr="aria-label:con.previewSize" aria-label="Preview size">
      <button type="button" data-prev-dev="wide" aria-pressed="true" data-i18n="emb.desktop">Desktop</button>
      <button type="button" data-prev-dev="phone" aria-pressed="false" data-i18n="emb.mobile">Mobile</button>
    </span>
    <a class="c-prev-open" id="cPrevOpen" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-i18n-attr="title:con.previewOpen,aria-label:con.previewOpen" title="Open in a new tab">&#8599;</a>
  </div>
  <p class="hint c-prev-gone" id="cPrevGone" hidden data-i18n="con.previewGone">This page is not built on this site yet — it is showing “coming soon”. Its preview is on dev.thauma.one.</p>
  {#- words with nothing to show them in yet: the app, the widgets -#}
  <p class="hint c-prev-none" id="cPrevNone" hidden data-i18n="con.noPreview">There is no preview of these words here yet.</p>
  <div class="c-prev-frame"><iframe id="cPrevFrame" title="Preview" data-i18n-attr="title:con.preview"></iframe></div>
</aside>
